flowchart TB
    accTitle: A topic per thing
    accDescr: A new thing, such as an alarm, a contribution or a release, opens a topic of its own in the chat, named after its repository and what it is. Its message with the buttons comes first, and its changes edit it there. Its drafts, the prompt of Edit, what Later brings back and the answers to what Dennis asks in the topic follow in it; his question goes to the control repository together with the thing. Once the thing is done, its topic gets a check mark in front of its name and stays. Without Threaded Mode, or when Telegram refuses the topic or a message in it, the thing goes on in the main view, as before.

    thing["A new thing: an alarm, a contribution, a release, code scanning"]
    open["`**createForumTopic** opens its topic, such as 🚨 demo needs you`"]
    first["`Its message with the buttons comes first; its changes edit it there`"]
    ask["`Dennis asks in the topic: the text goes to the control repository **with the thing**`"]
    more["`Drafts, ✏️ Edit, ⏰ Later and the answers follow in the topic`"]
    done["`**✅** in front of its name once it is done; the topic stays`"]
    main["`**Main view**, as before: no Threaded Mode, a refused topic or message, or a topic that is gone`"]

    thing --> open
    open --> first
    first -- "a question" --> ask
    ask -- "the answer" --> more
    first --> more
    more -- "merged, green again, ignored" --> done
    open -- "no topics, or Telegram refuses" --> main

    classDef you fill:#f59e0b2e,stroke:#f59e0b,stroke-width:2px
    classDef bot fill:#526cfe2e,stroke:#526cfe,stroke-width:2px
    classDef done fill:#16a34a2e,stroke:#16a34a,stroke-width:2px
    classDef warn fill:#dc26262e,stroke:#dc2626,stroke-width:2px
    class thing,ask you
    class open,first,more bot
    class done done
    class main warn
